==============================================================================
Both limbs of the inverted-U, measured separately
==============================================================================

113 hard-course control trials
   mean time above band      31.7%
   mean time strictly within  65.4%
   mean time below band       2.9%
   trials with ANY time below band: 32 of 113 (28%)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Does time on each side predict worse performance?
(both negative and significant = a genuine inverted-U)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  performance ~ pct_above
      pct_above   b = -0.180 [-0.271, -0.088]  p = 0.0001

  performance ~ pct_below
      pct_below   b = +0.038 [-0.298, +0.374]  p = 0.8250

  performance ~ pct_above + pct_below
      pct_above   b = -0.191 [-0.286, -0.097]  p = 0.0001
      pct_below   b = -0.156 [-0.482, +0.170]  p = 0.3487

